(footprint "SW_Push_Side_CTS_225B_7.8x3.5mm_Boss"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Side-actuated SMD tactile switch, 7.8 x 3.5 mm gull-wing with two locating bosses. Land pattern is the PCB LAYOUT from the CTS Series 225B datasheet (225BM...RB1(S)/RB2(S), 'Surface Mount, With Boss'), read out of the PDF as vector geometry rather than measured off a raster scan: pads 1/2 are 1.00 x 1.25 mm on 4.30 mm centres, the two SH pads are 1.50 x 1.20 mm on 6.80 mm centres, bosses on a 2.30 mm pitch. Origin sits midway between the two boss holes, which is the mechanical datum the bosses define; the part body centre is 0.15 mm off it, toward the pad 1/2 side. Pads 1 and 2 are the momentary switch. The datasheet's terminals 3 and 4 are permanently linked inside the part and it draws them tied to earth, so they are carried here as two pads both numbered SH, which pairs with the stock Switch:SW_Push_Shielded symbol and puts them on GND. They are the frame, and on a side-push they are what takes the actuation load. Boss holes are drilled 1.0 mm (the CTS figure, +0.1/-0) so that the same land accepts both a genuine CTS 225B, whose bosses are 0.8 mm, and the common unbranded 3.5 x 7.8 x 3.8 mm clone sold as a '3x6x3.8 with points' assortment part, whose bosses are 0.7 mm and whose own drawing calls for 0.9 mm holes. The clone's land pattern agrees with CTS to within 0.05 mm in X, and where the two differ in pad height this pattern takes the larger envelope, always growing pads away from the holes rather than toward them. Two dimensions are therefore deliberately 0.05 mm off the CTS figures and are not transcription slips: pads 1/2 sit on 4.30 mm centres rather than CTS's 4.20, which lines their inner edges up with the clone's 3.30 mm gap and buys the copper-to-hole-wall clearance back up to 0.207 mm, and the SH pads reach 0.05 mm further inboard than CTS's 5.40 mm inner span so they also cover the clone's 5.30. The outer span of 8.30 mm and the boss pitch match CTS exactly. The clone numbers its terminals the other way round, calling the linked frame 1/2 and the switch 3/4, which is a further reason the frame pads are labelled SH here rather than by number: on both parts the small inboard pads are the switch and the large outboard pads are the frame, so either part drops onto this footprint unchanged and there is no numbering left to get backwards. The actuator pushes toward +Y, drawn on F.Fab with an arrow: place this at a board edge with that edge facing the housing wall. Actuator length varies by part number (CTS orders it as 'L'), so the courtyard is drawn generously on the push side. No 3D model yet.")
	(tags "switch tactile side push smd boss cts 225b 7.8x3.5")
